 "standard_url": "https://www.thecorestandards.org/Math/Content/7/NS/A/3/",
 "standard_text": "Solve real-world and mathematical problems involving the four operations with rational numbers.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Grade 7 rational number word problems worksheets: choose the operation, then solve problems with integers, decimals, fractions and mixed numbers, including multi-step problems with money, temperature and elevation. 100 practice questions with an answer key.",
 "key_big": "Give each number a sign, choose the operation from the words, then solve.",
 "key_sub": "Gains are positive and losses are negative. Estimate first and check the sign of your answer.",
 "body_html": "<h2>Plan, then compute</h2><p>Read the problem and decide what each number means. Give gains a + sign and losses a − sign. Choose the operation from the words, then use the rules for integers, decimals and fractions.</p><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Words in the problem</th><th>Operation</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rises, gains, deposits</td><td>add a positive</td><td>−4 + 9 = 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls, loses, spends</td><td>add a negative (or subtract)</td><td>−4 + (−6) = −10</td></tr><tr><td>Difference or distance</td><td>subtract (distance is never negative)</td><td>12 − (−5) = 17</td></tr><tr><td>The same change many times</td><td>multiply</td><td>5 × (−3) = −15</td></tr><tr><td>Share or split equally, how many groups</td><td>divide</td><td>−24 ÷ 4 = −6, 6 ÷ <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span> = 8</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>The temperature is −6°F. It rises 2.5°F each hour for 6 hours. What is it then?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>The change is 6 × 2.5 = 15 degrees.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Add it to the start: −6 + 15 = 9.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 9°F</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Ruby has $50. She buys 3 books at $8.75 and a $4.50 bookmark. How much is left?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Books: 3 × 8.75 = 26.25.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Spent: 26.25 + 4.50 = 30.75.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Left: 50 − 30.75 = 19.25.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: $19.25</p></div><h2>Check your answer</h2><p>Estimate first: 3 books at about $9 is about $27, so about $18 to $20 is left. Check the sign: is the answer above or below zero, a gain or a loss?</p><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Wrong sign: a fall of 6 degrees from −4 is −10, not 2.</li><li>Stopping early: the question asks what is left, not what was spent.</li><li>Dividing the wrong way: how many <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span>-foot pieces in 6 feet is 6 ÷ <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span>, not <span class='fr'><span class='fn'>3</span><span class='fd'>4</span></span> ÷ 6.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "How do I know which operation to use?",
   "a": "Look at what the words mean. Rises, gains and deposits add; falls and losses add a negative; the same change many times multiplies; sharing equally divides."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is a rational number?",
   "a": "Any number that can be written as a fraction of two integers, such as −4, 2.5 (5/2) and −3/4."
  },
  {
   "q": "How can I check my answer?",
   "a": "Estimate with rounded numbers, check that the sign makes sense (above or below zero), and make sure you answered the question that was asked."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I solve a multi-step problem?",
   "a": "Break it into steps. Find each part, write it down, then combine. Ruby's books cost 3 × 8.75 = 26.25, then add the bookmark, then subtract from $50."
  }
 ],
